      "writtenOn": "2023-09-22T19:16:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does bazel reanalyze stuff / slow down in general when the symlink forest is deleted and recreated?\n\nCan we avoid having bazel reanalyze, and just have symlink forest rerun? (We run the symlink forest regenerator on a code change, but only touch each output if it has changed). \n\n\u003e If it causes bazel reanalysis I don\u0027t think it\u0027s worth doing this change.\n\nWhy? How frequently do you think this will happen? I anticipate that users will only experience such a reanalysis on a sync (with a build system change), which almost always results in a reanalysis anyway.\n\n\u003e You can just use symlinkForestVersion instead, maybe doing the LINT.ifChange thing.\n\nThis is a very manual option that I don\u0027t think is sufficient. symlink_forest.go is not a standalone binary -- it has a whole tree of dependencies, and if any of those dependencies change, it might cause a change in symlink forest regeneration. Enforcing LINT.ifChange is not sufficient to work around a correctness bug.\n\n1. LINT.ifChange would have to be applied on the entirety of build/soong and its dependencies to truly \n2. This does not prevent *local* changes causing correctness bugs, a potential source of confusion for local build system development.\n\nIt would be better for the build system to behave with correctness when possible, without such manual hacks. The approach of bumping a version manually with the build system changes is a decent hack for an expedient solution, or to cut corners in the name of efficiency, but we should investigate other approaches.",
      "parentUuid": "1e7eea89_1a1baa7d",
      "revId": "1adac7eaae08516ae7e95d983006b7c50cdb1229",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d21c3e2f_08ee7033",
        "filename": "bp2build/symlink_forest.go",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-22T20:48:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How frequently do you think this will happen?\n\nIt will happen on any change to soong, which is extremely frequently for soong developers. Though yes, regular users won\u0027t experience this much.\n\n\u003e LINT.ifChange would have to be applied on the entirety of build/soong\n\nWhile technically any soong change could affect the symlink forest, I was thinking you\u0027d just apply that to `symlink_forest.go`, which is the only file that\u0027s likely to cause issues.\n\n\u003e It would be better for the build system to behave with correctness when possible\n\nThe build system is already correct 100% of the time when there are no changes made by developers. Asking developers to bump the version number on the relevant changes seems in line with asking developers to not write bugs, which is reasonable.",
      "parentUuid": "436efc0d_d8c3fb94",
      "revId": "1adac7eaae08516ae7e95d983006b7c50cdb1229",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
